#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Uvod"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&jovie; is a subsystem within &kde; for producing Text-to-Speech (TTS). It "
"provides a common API for &kde; programmers to give TTS capabilities to "
"their applications. It provides some nice capabilities for end users as well."
msgstr ""
"&jovie; je podsistem unutar &kde; za stvaranje Tekst-u-govor (TUG). "
"Omogućuje uobičajeni API za &kde; programere kako bi njihove aplikacije "
"mogle koristiti TTS mogućnosti. Također nudi neke lijepe mogućnosti za "
"kranje korisnike."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "User features:"
msgstr "Korisničke značajke:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak contents of a text file."
msgstr "Govori sadržaj tekstualne datoteke."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak &kde; notification events (KNotify)."
msgstr "Govori &kde; obavijesti o događajima (KNotify)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak all or part of the text of a web page in &konqueror;."
msgstr "Govori cijeli ili dio teksta web stranice u &konqueror;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Speak all or part of the text in &kate; text editor, including instances "
"where &kate; is embedded in another &kde; application."
msgstr ""
"Govori cijeli ili dio teksta u &kate; tekstualnom editoru, uključujući i "
"slučajeve gdje je &kate; ugrađen u drugu &kde; aplikaciju."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Speech is spoken via speech-dispatcher, so any speech-dispatcher backend can "
"be used (espeak, festival, &etc;)"
msgstr ""
"Govor je emitovan preko govor-dispečera, pa se bilo koja govor-dispečer "
"pozadina može koristiti(espeak, festival, &etc;)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"User-configurable filters for substituting misspoken words, choosing speech "
"synthesizers, and transforming XHMTL/&XML; documents."
msgstr ""
"Korisnički podesiv filter za zamjenu pogrešno izgovorenih riječi, zamjenu "
"govornog sintisajzera, i transformaciju XHTML/&XML; dokumenata."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Programmer features:"
msgstr "Programerske značajke:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Priority system for screen reader outputs, warnings and messages, while "
"still playing regular texts."
msgstr ""
"Prioritetni sistem čitač zaslona, upozorenja i poruke, dok se u pozadini i "
"dalje reproducira regularan tekst."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Permit generation of speech from the command line (or via shell scripts) "
"using the &qdbus; utility."
msgstr ""
"Dozvoli generisanje govora iz komandne linije(ili preko shell skripte) "
"koristeći &qdbus; uslužni program."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Provide a lightweight and easily usable interface for applications to "
"generate speech output."
msgstr ""
"Osigurava lagano i lako upotrebljivo korisničko sučelje za aplikacije kako "
"bi mogle generisati govorni izlaz."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applications need not be concerned about contention over the speech device."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"FUTURE: Provide support for speech markup languages, such as VoiceXML, "
"Sable, &Java; Speech Markup Language (JSML), and Speech Markup Meta-language "
"(SMML)."
msgstr ""
"USKORO: Pružanje podrške za govorne jezike za označavanje, kao što su "
"VoiceXML, Sable, &Java; Speech Markup Language (JSML), i Speech Markup Meta-"
"language (SMML)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "FUTURE: Provide limited support for embedded speech markers."
msgstr "USKORO: Osiguravanje ograničene podrške za ugrađene govorne signale."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "Asynchronous to prevent system blocking."
msgstr "Asinhron, kako bi se spriječilo blokiranje sistema."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "&jovie; actually consists of several programs:"
msgstr "&jovie; zapravo se sastoji od nekoliko programa:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the &kde; Text-to-Speech Daemon, which is an application that provides TTS "
"services to applications via &DBus;. It also sits in the system tray."
msgstr ""
"&kde; Tekst-u-Govor Daemon, koji je aplikacija koja omogućuje TUG usluge "
"aplikaciji preko &DBus;. Također, nalazi se u traci sistema."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A plugin for the &konqueror; web browser that permits you to speak all or a "
"portion of the text on a web page."
msgstr ""
"Plugin za &konqueror; internet preglednik koji vam omogućuje da bude govoren "
"cijeli ili dio teksta web stranice."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A plugin for the &kate; text editor that permits you to speak all or a "
"portion of a text file."
msgstr ""
"Plugin za &kate; tekstualni editor koji vam omogućuje da bude govoren cijeli "
"ili samo dio tekstualne datoteke."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Support"
msgstr "Podrška"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to the &kde; Bugzilla database ( <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde."
"org/\">http://bugs.kde.org/</ulink> ), discussions for &jovie; currently "
"take place in the kde-accessibility mailing list. Subscribe at <ulink url="
"\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-accessibility\"> https://mail."
"kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-accessibility</ulink>. Developers also hang out "
"in IRC (irc.kde.org, channel #kde-accessibility)."
msgstr ""
"Osim &kde; Bugzilla baze podataka ( <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/"
"\">http://bugs.kde.org/</ulink> ), diskusija za &jovie; se trenutno odvija i "
"preko kde-accessibility liste za slanje pošte. Prijavite se na adresi <ulink "
"url=\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-accessibility\"> https://"
"mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-accessibility</ulink>. Programeri se "
"trenutno okupljaju na IRC (irc.kde.org, kanalu #kde-accessibility)."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &jovie;"
msgstr "Koristeći &jovie;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you can use &jovie;, you must install speech-dispatcher and make sure "
"it is working. See <xref linkend=\"installation\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Prije nego što možete koristiti &jovie;, morate instalirati govor-dispečer i "
"uvjeriti se da radi ispravno. Pogledajte  <xref linkend=\"installation\"/>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting <command>jovie</command>"
msgstr "Pokretanje <command>jovie</command>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "To start the &jovie; system, type the following command in a &konsole;"
msgstr "Da bi pokrenuli &jovie; sistem, utipkajte sljedeću komandu u &konsole;"

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:188 index.docbook:1139
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>jovie</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>jovie</userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "or click on &jovie; in the &kde; Menu."
msgstr "ili kliknite na &jovie; u &kde; Meniju."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is the first time running <command>jovie</command>, or if you have "
"not yet configured any talkers, the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> screen "
"appears. See <xref linkend=\"configure-talkers\"/>. If you have already "
"configured at least one talker, the <guilabel>General</guilabel> screen "
"appears. See <xref linkend=\"general\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ukoliko je ovo prvi put da pokrećete <command>jovie</command>, ili ukoliko "
"još niste podesili niti jedan govornik, <guilabel>Govornici</guilabel> "
"zaslon će se pojaviti. Pogledajte<xref linkend=\"configure-talkers\"/>. "
"Ukoliko ste već podesili barem jedan govornik,  <guilabel>Općenito</"
"guilabel>  zaslon će se pojaviti. Pogledajte  <xref linkend=\"general\"/>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Talkers"
msgstr "Podešavanje Govornika."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most text-to-speech (TTS) synthesizers offer multiple languages and voices "
"and may offer multiple speaking genders, volumes, and rates. You may "
"configure more than one instance of a synthesizer. Each combination of "
"language, synthesizer, voice, gender, volume, and rate is called a talker. "
"You should configure at least one talker before you use &jovie; otherwise "
"speech-dispatcher will use a default voice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multiple talkers for the same synthesizer is similar to multiple print "
"queues for a single physical printer."
msgstr ""
"Slučaj više govornika za isti sintesajzer je sličan slučaju više redova za "
"štampanje koji čekaju samo jedan štampač."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> tab in <command>jovie</"
"command>, the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> screen appears. This screen also "
"automatically appears if you start <command>jovie</command> and you have not "
"yet configured any talkers."
msgstr ""
"Kada kliknete <guilabel>Govornici</guilabel> tab u <command>jovie</command>, "
"pojavit će se <guilabel>Govornici</guilabel> zaslon. Ovaj zaslon se "
"automatski pojavljuje ako pokrenete <command>jovie</command> i ako još niste "
"podesili niti jedan govornik."

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Talkers tab)."
msgstr "&kde; Tekst-u-govor Upravitelj (Talkers tab)."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Talkers tab)"
msgstr "&kde; Tekst-u-Govor Upravitelj (Talkers tab)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click to add a new talker."
msgstr "Pritisnite da dodate novi govornik."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the configured <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> are listed here. Highest "
"priority <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> are listed at the top. The top-most "
"talker will be used to do the speaking when an application does not specify "
"a talker."
msgstr ""
"Svi podešeni <guilabel>Govornici</guilabel> su prikazani ovdje. "
"<guilabel>Govornici</guilabel> sa najvećim prioritetom su prikazani na vrhu. "
"Prvi na vrhu govornik će biti korišten za govor kada aplikacija ne "
"specificira govornika."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on a talker in the list to highlight it and click this button to "
"remove it."
msgstr ""
"Klikniite na govornik u listi da bi ga označili a zatim kliknite na ovo "
"dugme da ga uklonite."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on a talker in the list to highlight it and click this button to "
"change its configuration. See below."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite na govornik u listi da bi ga označili a zatim kliknite na ovo dugme "
"da bi ga podesili. Pogledajte ispod."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on a talker in the list to highlight it and click this button to move "
"it down one row in the list. The lower a talker appears in the list, the "
"lower its priority."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite na govornik u listi da bi ga označili a zatim kliknite na ovo dugme "
"da bi ga pomjerili za jedan red dolje u listi. Što se govornik nalazi niže u "
"listi, to je njegov prioritet manji."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click one of these buttons to apply the changes you have made to the running "
"&jovie; system."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite na jedan od ovih dugmadi da bi ste potvrdili promjene koje ste "
"napravili pokrenutom &jovie; sistemu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> button, the <guilabel>Add "
"Talker</guilabel> screen appears."
msgstr ""
"Kada kliknete na  <guibutton>Add</guibutton> dugme, the <guilabel>Dodaj "
"Govornik</guilabel> zaslon će se pojaviti."

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Talker screen."
msgstr "Dodaj Govornika zaslon."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Talker screen"
msgstr "Dodaj Govornika zaslon"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "You should give your new talker a name, this can be anything."
msgstr "Morate dati naziv novom govorniku, ime može biti bilo šta."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose the language and synthesizer here."
msgstr "Izaberite jezik i sintesajzer ovdje."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the voice type here, there are three Male, three Female, one Male "
"Child and one Female Child voices to choose from."
msgstr ""
"Ovdje izaberite vrstu glasa, možete birati između tri muška, tri ženska, "
"jednog muškog dječijeg i jednog ženskog dječijeg glasa."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set any custom voice parameters here."
msgstr "Postavite proizvoljne parametre za glas ovdje."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click here your new talker will appear in the list in the "
"<guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> screen. Click the <guibutton>Edit</guibutton> "
"button to edit the talker's configuration."
msgstr ""
"Kada kliknete ovdje, vaš novi govornik će se pojaviti u listi, u "
"<guilabel>Govornici</guilabel> zaslonu. Kliknite dugme <guibutton>Izmjeni</"
"guibutton> da bi ste izmjenili postavke govornika."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are almost ready to begin using &jovie;. Now go back to the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> tab and check the <guilabel>Enable Text-to-"
"Speech System (Jovie)</guilabel> box. This will start the &kde; TTS Daemon. "
"See <xref linkend=\"general\"/>. You may now begin using &jovie; to speak "
"text. Click the <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> tab to create and manage text "
"jobs. See <xref linkend=\"jobmgr\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Skoro ste spremni za korištenje &jovie;. Sada idite natrag na tab "
"<guilabel>Općenito</guilabel> i označite <guilabel>Omogući Tekst-u-Govor "
"Sistem(Jovie)</guilabel> okvir. Sada možete početi sa korištenjem &jovie; za "
"izgovor teksta. Kliknite na <guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> tab da bi ste "
"kreirali tekstualne poslove kao i upravljali njima. Pogledajte <xref linkend="
"\"jobmgr\"/>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &jovie; and Setting General Options"
msgstr "Pokretanje &jovie; i postavljanje općih opcija."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have configured at least one talker, you can start the &kde; Text-"
"to-Speech System. Click on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab. The "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> screen appears. You can also set some general "
"options on this screen."
msgstr ""
"Kada podesite barem jedan govornik, možete pokrenuti &kde; Tekst-u-Govor "
"sistem. Kliknite na tab <guilabel>Općenito</guilabel>. Pojavit će se zaslon "
"<guilabel>Općenito</guilabel>. Sada možete podesiti neke opće postavke na "
"ovom zaslonu."

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (General tab)."
msgstr "&kde; Tekst-u-Govor Upravitelj (Opećenito tab)."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (General tab)"
msgstr "&kde; Tekst-u-Govor Upravitelj (Opećenito tab)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this box to activate the &jovie; system. This starts the &kde; TTS "
"Daemon (&jovie;). If Jovie starts successfully, the <guilabel>Jobs</"
"guilabel> tab will appear. Once &jovie; has been started, you can begin "
"creating and speaking text jobs. See <xref linkend=\"jobmgr\"/>. Unchecking "
"will stop Jovie and deactivate the &kde; TTS system."
msgstr ""
"Označite ovaj okvir da bi ste aktivirali &jovie; sistem. Ovo će započeti "
"&kde; TUG Daemon (&jovie;). Ako se Jovie pokrene uspješno, tab "
"<guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> će se pojaviti. Jednom kada je &jovie; "
"pokrenut, možete započeti sa kreiranjem novih poslova i govorom postojećih "
"tekstualnih poslova. Pogledajte <xref linkend=\"jobmgr\"/>. Odznačavanje "
"okvira će zaustaviti Jovie i deaktivirati &kde; TUG sistem."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Be sure to click here to save your settings."
msgstr "Ne zaboravite da kliknete ovdje da sačuvate vaše postavke."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing Text Jobs"
msgstr "Upravljanje Tekstualnim Poslovima"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click the <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> tab in <command>jovie</"
"command>, the <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> screen appears."
msgstr ""
"Kada kliknete na <guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> tab u <command>jovie</"
"command>, pojavit će se <guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> zaslon."

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Jobs tab)."
msgstr "&kde; Tekst-u-Govor Upravitelj(Poslovi tab)."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Jobs tab)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The controls here allow you to change attributes of the currently speaking "
"voice. Note this only works if you have no voices configured in the Talkers "
"tab."
msgstr ""
"Kontrole ovdje će vam omogućiti da promjenite atribute trenutnog govornog "
"glasa. Napomena, ovo radi samo ukoliko niste podesili niti jedan glas u tabu "
"Govornici."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The buttons in this row permit you to stop, cancel, pause and resume the "
"current text job."
msgstr ""
"Dugmadi u ovom redu vam omogućuju da zaustavite, ukinete, pauzirate i "
"nastavite trenutni tekstualni posao."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The buttons in this row permit you to speak the text currently in the &kde; "
"clipboard, or open a text file for speaking. You can also change the talker "
"for a job."
msgstr ""
"Dugmadi u ovom redu vam omogućuju da se reproducira tekst koji se trenutno "
"nalazi u &kde; međuspremniku, ili da otvorite tekstualnu datoteku kako bi se "
"reproducirala. Također, možete promjeniti govornika za ovaj posao."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> or <guibutton>Apply</guibutton>, "
"all changes to settings on other screens are applied (if any)."
msgstr ""
"Kada kliknete na dugme<guibutton>OK</guibutton> ili <guibutton>Primijeni "
"postavke</guibutton>, sve promjene u postavkama na drugim zaslonima će biti "
"primijenjene(ukoliko takve postoje)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> tab only appears when &jovie; is running. If "
"you do not see the <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> tab, click on the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> tab and check the <guilabel>Enable Text-to-"
"Speech (Jovie)</guilabel> box."
msgstr ""
"Tab <guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> će se pojaviti samo kada je &jovie; već "
"pokrenut.  Ukoliko ne vidite <guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> tab, kliknite na "
"tab <guilabel>Općenito</guilabel> i označite <guilabel>Omogući Tekst-u-Govor "
"(Jovie)</guilabel> okvir."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speaking Text from Web Pages"
msgstr "Govorenje teksta sa web stranica."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While running the &kde; &konqueror; web browser, you can speak the text of "
"the web page displayed. First ensure that &jovie; is running. Highlight the "
"text you want spoken and choose <menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Tools</guisubmenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Speak Text</guisubmenu> </menuchoice> on the main menu. "
"<action>After a moment, the highlighted text should begin speaking.</action>"
msgstr ""
"Dok je pokrenut &kde; &konqueror; internet preglednik, možete pokrenuti "
"govorenje teksta web stranice koja je prikazana. Prvo se uvjerite da je "
"&jovie; pokrenut. Označite tekst koji želite da se govori i izaberite "
"<menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Alati</guisubmenu> <guisubmenu>Govori Tekst</"
"guisubmenu> </menuchoice> na glavnom meniju. <action>Nedugo zatim, označeni "
"tekst će biti reproduciran.</action>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is almost always a good idea to highlight the text on the web page you "
"want spoken. You can skip this step, but you will hear a lot of &HTML; "
"headers and other invisible tags spoken."
msgstr ""
"Gotovo uvijek, dobra ideja je da označite tekst na web stranici koji želite "
"da se govori. Možete preskočiti ovaj korak, ali ćete čuti dosta izgovorenih "
"&HTML; zaglavlja kao i drugih nevidljivih tagova."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speaking Text from &kate; Text Editor"
msgstr "Govorenje teksta iz &kate; Tekstualnog editora."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While running the &kde; Advanced Text Editor (&kate;), you can speak the "
"text displayed. First ensure that &jovie; is running and enable the "
"<guilabel>KTextEditor Jovie Text-to-Speech Plugin</guilabel> in &kate;'s "
"settings dialog. Highlight the text you want spoken and choose <menuchoice> "
"<guisubmenu>Tools</guisubmenu> <guisubmenu>Speak Text</guisubmenu> </"
"menuchoice> on the main menu. <action>After a moment, the highlighted text "
"should begin speaking.</action>"
msgstr ""
"Dok je pokrenut &kde; Advanced Text Editor (&kate;), možete omogućiti "
"govorenje označenog teksta. Prvo se uvjerite da je &jovie; pokrenut i "
"aktivirajte  <guilabel>KTextEditor Jovie Text-u-Govor Plugin</guilabel> u "
"&kate; postavkama. Označite tekst koji želite da se govori i izaberite  "
"<menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Alati</guisubmenu> <guisubmenu>Govori Tekst</"
"guisubmenu> </menuchoice> u glavnom meniju. <action>Nedugo zatim, označeni "
"tekst će biti reproduciran.</action>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You do not have to first highlight text. In this case, the entire file will "
"be spoken."
msgstr ""
"Niste obavezni da prvo označite tekst. U tom slučaju, cijela tekstualna "
"datoteka će biti reproducirana."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This also works when &kate; is running embedded in another application, such "
"as &konqueror; or &quanta;."
msgstr ""
"Ovo također radi kada je &kate; pokrenut kao sastavni dio neke druge "
"aplikacije, kao što je &konqueror; ili &quanta;."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speaking Notifications (KNotify)"
msgstr "Govorenje obavijesti (KNotify)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"KNotify is the notification subsystem within &kde;, which alerts you to "
"events you configure within the &kde; system. You can configure &jovie; to "
"speak text notifications."
msgstr ""
"KNotify je podsistem za obavijesti unutar &kde;, koji vas upozorava na "
"događaje koje podešavate unutar &kde; sistema. Također možete podesiti "
"&jovie; da govori i notifikacije."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, &konversation;, a &kde; IRC application, permits you to "
"configure a wide variety of notifications. For instance, you can tell "
"&konversation; to notify you whenever a message appears in an IRC channel "
"with your nickname in it. Together with &jovie; you can have &kde; speak the "
"text of the IRC message to you."
msgstr ""
"Na primjer, &konversation;, &kde; IRC aplikacija, omogućuje vam da podesite "
"širok izbor obavijesti. Na primjer, možete narediti &konversation; da vas "
"obavijesti kada god se pojavi nova poruka koja sadrži vaš nadimak, na IRC "
"kanalu. Zajedno sa &jovie; možete imati  i &kde; i tako možete omogućiti da "
"se reproduciraju IRC poruke."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In general, if a &kde; application supports KNotify, a "
"<guilabel>Notifications</guilabel> menu item will appear under the "
"application's <guilabel>Settings</guilabel> menu. The specifics for "
"configuring each application with KNotify vary from application to "
"application."
msgstr ""
"U globalu, ako &kde; aplikacija podržava KNotify, a <guilabel>Obavijesti</"
"guilabel> meni će se pojaviti unutar menija  <guilabel>Postavke</guilabel>. "
"Podaci za podešavanja pojedinačnih aplikacija koje posjeduju KNotify, "
"razlikuju se od aplikacije do aplikacije."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"String Replacer filters are a good way to clean up messages sent from "
"applications if they are mispronounced or misspoken in &jovie;. The "
"<filename>kmail.xml</filename> file, which comes with &jovie;, is a good "
"example. It removes <command>br</command>, and <command>b</command> tags "
"from the &kmail; notification messages and also removes the phrase <command>/"
"local/inbox/</command>, since this may be safely assumed in most cases. See "
"<xref linkend=\"stringreplacer\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Filteri za zamijenu rečenica su dobar način da očistite poruke su poslane od "
"strane aplikacije, ukoliko su pogrešno izgovorene u &jovie;. Fajl "
"<filename>kmail.xml</filename>, koji dolazi sa &jovie; <command>/local/inbox/"
"</command>, jer se ovo može sigurno predpostaviti u većini slučajeva. "
"Pogledajte <xref linkend=\"stringreplacer\"/>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filters (Advanced)"
msgstr "Filteri(Napredno)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:530
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filters are an advanced feature of &jovie;. For the basic operation of "
"&jovie;, they are not needed."
msgstr ""
"Filteri su napredna značajka &jovie;. Oni nisu potrebni za osnovne operacije "
"&jovie;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filters are used to pre-process text before it is sent to speech-dispatcher. "
"They are useful for enhancing speech, substituting for misspoken words or "
"abbreviations, choosing the appropriate language and talker to do the "
"speaking, or working around certain limitations of speech synthesizers and "
"their voices."
msgstr ""
"Filteri se koriste za pre-procesuiranje teksta, prije no što se on pošalje "
"govor-dispečeru. Vrlo su korisni za poboljšanje govora, zamjenu pogrešno "
"izgovorenih riječi ili skraćenica, izbor odgovarajućeg jezika i govornika "
"koji će se koristit za govor. Također su vrlo korisni za prevazilaženje "
"određenih ograničenja koje postavljaju govorni sintisajzer i njihovi glasovi."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid "Types of &jovie; Messages"
msgstr "Tipovi &jovie; Poruka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To understand how to use filters, it is helpful to first understand how text "
"is processed by speech-dispatcher. Text spoken by &jovie; is of four "
"possible types."
msgstr ""
"Da bi razumjeli kako se koriste filteri, korisno je da prvo shvatite kako "
"govor-dispečer procesuira tekst. Tekst izgovoren od &jovie; je jedan od "
"četiri moguća tipa."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen Reader Output."
msgstr "Izlaz čitača sadržaja zaslona."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid "Warnings."
msgstr "Upozorenja."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "Messages"
msgstr "Poruke"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Jobs"
msgstr "Poslovi"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The type is determined by the application that sends the text to &jovie;."
msgstr "Tip je određen na osnovu aplikacije koja šalje tekst &jovie;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Screen Reader Output has the highest priority. It is reserved for use by "
"Screen Reader applications. Screen Reader Output preempts all other "
"messages, causing those jobs to pause. Once the Screen Reader Output has "
"been spoken, the preempted messages will automatically resume."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Warnings are the next highest priority. It is reserved for high-priority "
"messages, such as \"CPU is over-heating.\" A Warning will preempt Messages "
"and regular text, causing those jobs to pause. Once the Warning has been "
"spoken, the preempted messages will automatically resume."
msgstr ""
"Upozorenja su sljedeći najveći prioritet. Namijenjena su za poruke visokog "
"prirotiteta kao što su \"CPU se pregrijava.\" Upozorenje će preduhitriti "
"Poruke i uobičajeni tekst te će zaustaviti ta dva posla. Jednom kada je "
"upozorenje izgovoreno, emitovanje poruka koje su bile aktivne prije toga će "
"automatski nastaviti."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Messages are the next highest priority. A Message will preempt regular text "
"jobs. &kmouth; is an example of an application that uses Messages. For "
"example, while reading out long text from a web page, &kmouth; can be used "
"to greet someone who walks into the room. &kde; Notifications are also "
"Messages (see <xref linkend=\"knotify\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The rest are ordinary Text Jobs. Any job you initiate from the "
"<guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> tab is a Text Job. KSayit is an example of an "
"application that uses Text Jobs. Text Jobs are intended for longer speech "
"output that is not urgent."
msgstr ""
"Ostatak su obični tekstualni poslovi. Svaki posao koji pokrenete iz taba "
"<guilabel>Poslovi</guilabel> je tekstualni posao. KSayit je primjer "
"aplikacije koja koristi tekstualne poslove. Ti poslovi su namijenjeni za "
"duže govore koji nisu hitni."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All four kinds of jobs are queues, except for Screen Reader Output. If a "
"Screen Reader Output is sent from an application while &jovie; is speaking "
"another Screen Reader Output, the speaking message is stopped and discarded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid "Types of Filters"
msgstr "Tipovi Filtera"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first thing you must know about filters is that they are never applied "
"to Screen Reader Output. They are applied to Warnings, Messages, and Text "
"jobs, and also &kde; notifications (KNotify)."
msgstr ""
"Prva stvar koju morate znati o filterima je da se oni nikad ne primjenjuju "
"na izlaz čitača zaslona. Oni se primjenjuju na upozorenja, poruka i "
"tekstualne poslove i također na &kde; obavještenja(KNotify)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filters process the text and pass it on to the next filter. There are "
"currently three kinds of filters."
msgstr ""
"Filteri obrađuju tekst i šalju ga dalje sljedećem filteru. Trenutno postoje "
"tri vrste filtera."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "String Replacers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid "&XML; Transformers"
msgstr "&XML; Preobrazivači"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "Talker Choosers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filters are implemented using a plugin architecture. In the future, there "
"may be additional kinds of filters."
msgstr ""
"Filteri su implementirani korištenjem plugin arhitekture. U budućnosti, može "
"biti dodadno još različitih vrsta filtera."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"String Replacer filters substitute pieces of text with other text. The "
"replaced pieces are matched either as words or as regular expressions. "
"&jovie; comes with pre-defined String Replacer filters for speaking "
"abbreviations, speaking chat emoticons, such as \":-)\", or reformatting "
"notification messages from &konversation; or &kmail; into a more "
"understandable form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:622
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&XML; Transformers use an &XML; Style Language - Transforms (XSLT) file to "
"convert &XML; of one format to another format. &jovie; comes with a couple "
"of XSLT files for converting &XHTML; into SSML."
msgstr ""
"&XML; Preobrazivači koriste &XML; Style Language - Transforms (XSLT) "
"datoteku da pretvore &XML; iz jednog formata u drugi. &jovie; dolazi sa "
"nekoliko XSLT datoteka za pretvaranje &XHTML; u SSML."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Talker Choosers permit you redirect jobs to a talker based on the contents "
"of the text, or upon the application that sent it to &jovie;. For example, "
"if you have configured a female talker in the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> "
"tab, you can direct text coming from KSayIt to that talker. See <xref "
"linkend=\"configure-talkers\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each of these kinds of filters has configurable rules for when the filter "
"should apply itself to the text to be spoken. If the filter determines that "
"it should not apply itself, the text is passed on to the next filter "
"unaltered."
msgstr ""
"Svaki od ovih filtera posjeduje izmjenjiva pravila koja govore kada će se "
"filter aktivirati na izgovarani tekst. Ukoliko filter zaključi da se ne "
"treba aktivirati, onda se neizmijenjeni tekst šalje dalje, na sljedeći "
"filter."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a Text Job, Message, Warning, or &kde; Notification message is sent to "
"&jovie;, it passes through each of the enabled filters you have configured "
"in the screen below. The order is from top to bottom."
msgstr ""
"Kada su tekstualni posao, Poruka,Upozorenje ili &kde; Obaviještenje poslani "
"ka &jovie;, on prolazi kroz svaki od aktivnih filtera koje ste podesili na "
"zaslonu ispod. Poredak je od vrha ka dnu."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Filters"
msgstr "Podešavanje Filtera"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use filters, click the <guilabel>Filters</guilabel> tab in "
"<command>jovie</command>."
msgstr ""
"Da bi ste koristili filtere, kliknite na <guilabel>Filteri</guilabel> tab u "
"<command>jovie</command>."

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:656
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Filters tab)."
msgstr "&kde; Tekst-u-Govor Upravitelj (Filteri tab)."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Filters tab)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the list of configured ordinary filters. If unchecked, the filter is "
"inactive and will be bypassed. Filters are applied in the order specified "
"here, top to bottom."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je lista podešenih uobičajenih filtera. Ukoliko odznačite neki filter, "
"on će biti neaktivan i bit će zaobiđen. Filteri se primjenjuju po redu "
"definisanom ovdje, od vrha prema dnu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click here to add a new filter. You will be prompted for the kind of filter "
"to add. After choosing the kind, see the configuration dialogs below."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite ovdje da dodate novi filter. Bit ćete upitani kakvu vrstu novog "
"filtera želite dodati. Nakon što izaberete vrstu, pogledajte ispod dijaloški "
"okvir za podešavanje postavki."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click here to remove a filter."
msgstr "Kliknite ovdje da uklonite filter."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:687
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click here to change the configuration of a filter. See the configuration "
"dialogs below."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite ovdje da promijenite podešavanja filtera. Pogledajte ispod "
"dijaloški okvir za podešavanje."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click these buttons to move a filter up or down in the list."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite na ovu dugmad da pomjerit filter za jedno mjesto gore ili dolje."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "Be sure to click here, otherwise your settings will not take effect."
msgstr "Ne zaboravite kliknuti ovdje, inače vaše postavke neće imati utjecaja."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring String Replacer Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:703
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You configure String Replacer filters by supplying a list of words or "
"regular expressions to be matched. When the matched words or regular "
"expressions are found in the text, each is replaced by a substitute string "
"you supply."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>String Replacer</screeninfo>"
msgstr "<screeninfo>Zamijenjivač rečenice</screeninfo>"

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>String Replacer</phrase>"
msgstr "<phrase>Zamijenjivač rečenice</phrase>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:737 index.docbook:836 index.docbook:921
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter a name for your filter. Use any name you like that distinguishes it "
"from all other filters."
msgstr ""
"Unesite ime za vaš filter. Koristite proizvoljno ime koje se razlikuje od "
"imena ostalih filtera."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:739
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the list of words and regular expressions. The filter searches for "
"matches on each string in the <guilabel>Match</guilabel> column, replacing "
"the matched string with the string in the <guilabel>Replace With</guilabel> "
"column. The list is processed in the order displayed, top to bottom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:744
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click here to add another word or regular expression to the list."
msgstr "Kliknite ovdje da dodate novu riječ ili novi uobičajeni izraz u listu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click here to move the currently highlighted word or regular expression up "
"or down in the list."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite ovdje da pomjerite trenutno označenu riječ ili uobičajeni izraz, "
"gore ili dolje u listi."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click to change an existing word or regular expression in the list."
msgstr "Kliknite da promijenite postojeću riječ ili uobičajeni izraz, u listi."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:750
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click to remove the currently highlighted word or regular expression from "
"the list."
msgstr ""
"Kliknite da uklonite trenutno označenu riječ ili uobičajeni izraz, iz liste."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these buttons to load a list of words or regular expression from a file, "
"save the current list to a file, or clear the entire list. When loading from "
"a file, the items in the file are appended to the existing list."
msgstr ""
"Koristite ovu dugmad da učitate listu riječi ili uobičajenih izraza iz "
"datoteke, sačuvate trenutnu listu u datoteku, ili da očistite cijelu listu. "
"Kada učitajete iz datoteke, stavke iz datoteke će biti dodane na postojeću "
"listu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:756
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not blank, the filter will apply itself only if the job's talker language "
"matches the language you enter here. Click the button to display a list of "
"languages. You may select more than one language by pressing &Ctrl; while "
"clicking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:761 index.docbook:852 index.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not blank, the filter will apply itself only if the text came from one of "
"the applications listed. You may enter more than one application separated "
"by commas. Example: <command><userinput>konversation,kmail</userinput></"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:765 index.docbook:856 index.docbook:934
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can discover the <guilabel>Application ID</guilabel> of running programs "
"using the <command>&qdbus;</command> program. You should leave the &DBus; "
"numbers out. For example, if &qdbus; shows an Application ID of "
"<command>kopete-3432</command>, you would just enter "
"<command><userinput>kopete</userinput></command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:773
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The String Replacer filter will only apply itself to the text if all non-"
"blank conditions are met in the <guilabel>Apply This Filter When</guilabel> "
"box. If all the boxes are blank, the filter will apply to all text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:778
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When matching words, the String Replacer filter internally uses a regular "
"expression of the form <command>\\s<userinput>word</userinput>\\s</command>. "
"In other words, the word must have word boundaries (spaces) on either side "
"of it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A discussion on how to write regular expressions is outside the scope of "
"this handbook. If you have the &kde; Regular Expression editor installed, "
"there is a button available on the <guilabel>Add</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Edit</guilabel> screens that will assist you at constructing "
"regular expressions. The &kde; Regular Expression Editor is part of the "
"Utils Git module in playground."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:789
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&jovie; comes with a few word list files, including a list of emoticons, "
"such as \":-)\", some abbreviations typically used in IRC or instant "
"messaging applications, and a list of other abbreviations. There is also a "
"list of special characters which the current version of the Polish Festival "
"voice cannot handle. If you develop useful word lists of your own, use the "
"<guibutton>Save</guibutton> button to save them to a file and send them to "
"the &jovie; team for inclusion in the next version."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &XML; Transformer Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:805
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &XML; Transformer filter uses XSLT files to transform &XML; from one "
"format to another. XSLT, the &XML; Style Language - Transforms, is a W3C "
"standard language for performing such transformations. It can only be used "
"on well-formed &XML;. You must have the <command>xsltproc</command> utility "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:813
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&XML; Transformer</screeninfo>"
msgstr "<screeninfo>&XML; Preobrazivač</screeninfo>"

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:828
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&XML; Transformer</phrase>"
msgstr "<phrase>&XML; Preobrazivač</phrase>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:838
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the full path to an existing XSLT file, which will perform the "
"transformation."
msgstr ""
"Unesite punu putanju za postojeću XSLT datoteku, koja će izvršiti preobrazbu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:840
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specify the path to the <command>xsltproc</command> utility. If xsltproc is "
"in your environment PATH, simply enter <command><userinput>xsltproc</"
"userinput></command>."
msgstr ""
"Specifirajte putanju za <command>xsltproc</command> uslužni program. Ukoliko "
"se xsltproc nalazi u vašoj environment putanji, jednostavno ukucajte "
"<command><userinput>xsltproc</userinput></command>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:843
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not blank, the filter will apply itself only if the &XML; has the "
"specified root element or a <command><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE]]></command> "
"specification beginning with the entered string. This distinguishes one form "
"of &XML; from another. For example, <command><userinput>html</userinput></"
"command> in the <guilabel>DOCTYPE</guilabel> box will match <command><!"
"[CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN\" \"http://"
"www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd\">]]></command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:864
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &XML; Transformer filter will only apply itself to the text if the "
"specified root element or DOCTYPE are met and if the application ID is met "
"in the <guilabel>Apply This Filter When</guilabel> box. If an item in this "
"box is blank, the test is not performed, so if all the boxes are blank, the "
"filter will apply itself to all text. However, you should fill in at least "
"one box, since many text jobs will not be in &XML; format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:878
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Talker Chooser Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:880
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Talker Chooser filters are used to direct the text to a desired talker "
"configured in the <guilabel>Talker</guilabel> tab, or to any talker having "
"specified attributes. For example, you can specify that text coming from "
"<command>kmail</command> should be spoken using a talker configured with a "
"female voice. See <xref linkend=\"configure-talkers\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:887
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just before &jovie; begins sending text to each of the filters, it picks a "
"talker to speak the text. The talker chosen is based on the talker "
"attributes specified by the application that sent the text to &jovie; and "
"the attributes of the talkers that you have configured on the "
"<guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> tab. The Talker Chooser filter permits you to "
"override the chosen talker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Talker Chooser</screeninfo>"
msgstr "<screeninfo>Izbor Govornika</screeninfo>"

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Talker Chooser</phrase>"
msgstr "<phrase>Izbor Govornika</phrase>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not blank, the filter will apply itself only if the text contains the "
"entered regular expression. If it is installed, click the browse button to "
"launch the &kde; Regular Expression Editor to assist you at entering the "
"regular expression."
msgstr ""
"Ukoliko nije prazan, filter će se sam aktivirati i primjeniti jedino ako "
"tekst sadrži unesene uobičajene izraze. Ukoliko je instaliran, kliknite na "
"dugme browse da pokrenete &kde; Editor Uobičajenih Izraza koji će vam pomoći "
"prilikom unosa novih uobičajenih izraza."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:927
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For better performance, try to \"anchor\" the regular expression to the "
"start of the string. In other words, start your regular expression with "
"<command><userinput><![CDATA[^]]></userinput></command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:939
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specify the attributes of the talker you prefer to speak the text here. If "
"the text meets the filter conditions above, a talker will be chosen that "
"most closely matches the attributes you specify here. Click the button at "
"the right to display the <guilabel>Select Talker</guilabel> screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:945
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these buttons to save your Talker Chooser settings, load settings from a "
"saved file, or clear all the settings."
msgstr ""
"Koristite ovu dugmad da bi ste sačuvali postavke Izbora Govornika, učitali "
"postavke iz snimljene datoteke, ili obrisali sve postavke."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:951
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Talker Chooser filter will only apply itself to the text if all non-"
"blank conditions are met in the <guilabel>Apply This Filter When</guilabel> "
"box. You must fill in at least one of the boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Developer's Guide to &jovie;"
msgstr "Programerski Vodič za &jovie;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1105
#, no-c-format
msgid "&jovie; has two Application Programmer Interfaces (APIs):"
msgstr "&jovie; ima dva Aplikativna programska interfejsa (API)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; Text-to-Speech API, which is used by application programmers to "
"give their applications TTS capabilities. Applications communicate with "
"&jovie; via &DBus;."
msgstr ""
"&kde; Tekst-u-Govor API, koji se koristi od strane programera kako bi "
"njihova aplikacija posjedovala TUG mogućnosti. Aplikacije također "
"komuniciraju sa &jovie; preko &DBus;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &jovie; Text-to-Speech Plugin API, which is used to add speech synthesis "
"plugins to &jovie; so that &jovie; will work with a new speech synthesis "
"engine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following section gives a short description of the &kde; Text-to-Speech "
"API &DBus; Interface. Full documentation for both APIs is available online "
"at the <ulink url=\"http://accessibility.kde.org/developer/kttsd/\"> &kde; "
"Accessibility</ulink> web site (http://accessibility.kde.org)."
msgstr ""
"Ova sekcija daje kratak opis za &kde; Tekst-u-Govor API &DBus; Intefejs. "
"Potpuna dokumentacija za oba API je dostupna na internetu na sljedećoj "
"adresi  <ulink url=\"http://accessibility.kde.org/developer/kttsd/\"> &kde; "
"Pristupačnost</ulink> internet stranica (http://accessibility.kde.org)."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1129
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &jovie; &DBus; Interface"
msgstr "The &jovie; &DBus; Interfejs"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applications communicate requests for Text-to-Speech services via the &kde; "
"&DBus; interface to program <command>jovie</command> object "
"<command>KSpeech</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1135
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the following commands in a &konsole;."
msgstr "Unesite sljedeću naredbu u &konsole;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid "If &jovie; is not already running"
msgstr "Ukoliko &jovie; nije već pokrenut"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1141
#, no-c-format
msgid "To queue a text job to be spoken"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:1143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"qdbus org.kde.jovie /KSpeech say \"<replaceable>text</replaceable>\" "
"\"<replaceable>options</replaceable>\""
msgstr ""
"qdbus org.kde.jovie /KSpeech say\"<replaceable>text</replaceable>\" "
"\"<replaceable>opcije</replaceable>\""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"where <userinput><replaceable>text</replaceable></userinput> is the text to "
"be spoken, and <userinput><replaceable>options</replaceable></userinput> is "
"a language code such as <userinput><replaceable>en</replaceable></"
"userinput>, <userinput><replaceable>cy</replaceable></userinput>, &etc;"
msgstr ""
"gdje<userinput><replaceable>tekst</replaceable></userinput> je tekst koji se "
"treba izgovarati i  <userinput><replaceable>opcije</replaceable></userinput> "
"je kod za jezik, na primjer <userinput><replaceable>en</replaceable></"
"userinput>, <userinput><replaceable>cy</replaceable></userinput>, &etc;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example."
msgstr "Primjer."

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:1150
#, no-c-format
msgid "qdbus org.kde.jovie /KSpeech say \"This is a test.\" \"en\""
msgstr "qdbus org.kde.jovie /KSpeech say \"This is a test.\" \"en\""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are many more commands that can be sent. To see a list of possible "
"commands,"
msgstr ""
"Postoji još mnogo naredbi koje možete poslati. Da bi ste vidjeli spisak "
"naredbi,"

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid "qdbus org.kde.jovie /KSpeech"
msgstr "qdbus org.kde.jovie /KSpeech"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or read the <ulink url=\"http://accessibility.kde.org/developer/kttsd/\"> "
"&kde; Text-to-Speech API</ulink> online."
msgstr ""
"ili pročitajte <ulink url=\"http://accessibility.kde.org/developer/kttsd/\"> "
"&kde; Tekst-u-Govor API</ulink> na internetu."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Pitanja i Odgovori"

#. Tag: chapter
#: index.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid "&reporting.bugs; &updating.documentation;"
msgstr "&reporting.bugs; &updating.documentation;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid "I need to start over. How do I get &jovie; completely terminated?"
msgstr "Moramo početi ispočetka. Kako da u potpunosti ugasim &jovie;?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1179
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the following commands in a &konsole;:"
msgstr "Unesite sljedeću naredbu u &konsole;:"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:1180
#, no-c-format
msgid "kquitapp jovie"
msgstr "kquitapp jovie"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1186
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I see debugging output from <command>jovie</command>?"
msgstr ""
"Kako mogu vidjeti izlaz za otklanjanje grešaka iz <command>jovie</command>?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open a &konsole; window. Then start <command>jovie</command>."
msgstr "Otvorite &konsole; prozor. Zatim pokrenite <command>jovie</command>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"None of the supported speech synthesizers support the language I need. Where "
"can I get a synth for my language?"
msgstr ""
"Niti jedan od podržanih govornih sintisajzer ne nudi jezik koji trebam. Gdje "
"mogu nabaviti sintisajzer za moj jezik?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Google(tm) is your friend. This <ulink url=\"http://tcts.fpms.ac.be/"
"synthesis/mbrola/mbrtts.html\">link</ulink> might also help. If you find a "
"free synthesis engine that supports your desired language, and want to add "
"support for it to &jovie;, please contact the development team. Open source "
"engines are especially welcome. If you know of a commercial synth, perhaps "
"you can persuade the vendor to donate a free copy to the &jovie; development "
"team. In the meantime, you may be able to get the synth working using speech-"
"dispatchers command backend."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have the &HTML; &XML; Transformer filter configured, but web pages are not "
"spoken at all using the Festival plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Due to a bug in Festival 1.95 beta, you must install the "
"<command>rab_diphone</command> (British male) voice for SABLE to work at "
"all, even if you are not using that voice to speak the web pages. Also, make "
"sure the <command>xsltproc</command> utility is installed and in the PATH."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Certain characters or punctuation seem to be producing errors in the "
"synthesizer, making it skip entire sentences, or pronounce gibberish. What "
"can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, make sure the <guilabel>Character encoding</guilabel> option in the "
"talker's configuration dialog is properly set for the language. If certain "
"words or characters are causing problems, a String Replacer filter might "
"help. See <xref linkend=\"filters\"/>."
msgstr ""

